## AWS EC2 — Dedicated Instance & Dedicated Host

### 1. Dedicated Instance

**Meaning:** EC2 instance runs on **hardware dedicated to your AWS account**.

```text
Normal EC2:
Physical Host
├── Your EC2
├── Other customer EC2
└── Other customer EC2

Dedicated Instance:
Physical Host
├── Your EC2
└── Your EC2
```

**Use when:**

* Physical hardware must be dedicated to your account.
* Organizational/compliance requirements require hardware isolation.

**Important:** It does **not automatically provide better performance, HA, or security** than normal EC2.

---

### 2. Dedicated Host

**Meaning:** You get an **entire physical server dedicated to your AWS account**.

```text
Dedicated Host
┌──────────────────────────┐
│ Physical AWS Server      │
│                          │
│ EC2   EC2   EC2          │
│                          │
│ Entire host = your AWS account
└──────────────────────────┘
```

**Use when:**

* Software licensing is tied to **physical hardware**.
* BYOL (**Bring Your Own License**) requirements.
* License depends on **physical sockets/cores**.
* You need visibility/control at the physical host level.

---

### Dedicated Instance vs Dedicated Host

|                               | Dedicated Instance         | Dedicated Host    |
| ----------------------------- | -------------------------- | ----------------- |
| Dedicated physical hardware   | ✅                          | ✅                 |
| Entire physical server        | ❌                          | ✅                 |
| Allocate host first           | ❌                          | ✅                 |
| Host-level control/visibility | Limited                    | ✅                 |
| BYOL / physical licensing     | Limited/use-case dependent | ⭐ Common use case |
| Normal application benefit    | Usually little             | Usually little    |

### 🧠 SAA Exam Memory

> **Dedicated Instance = Dedicated hardware**

> **Dedicated Host = Entire physical server**

> **Physical CPU/socket/server-based licensing → Think Dedicated Host**

### Console

**Dedicated Instance:**

`EC2 → Launch Instance → Advanced details → Tenancy → Dedicated`

**Dedicated Host:**

`EC2 → Dedicated Hosts → Allocate Dedicated Host → Launch EC2 → Tenancy = Dedicated Host`

**Don't confuse:** Dedicated ≠ automatically higher availability. For HA, think **multiple AZs + Auto Scaling / appropriate architecture**.


